/* ZAISRV binder source - 08-08's updated version (adds pingZaisrv).
   See solutions/08-08/zaisrv.rpgle for the implementation, and
   solutions/07-05/zaisrv.bnd for the ORIGINAL (3-procedure,
   PGMLVL(*CURRENT)-only) binder source this file replaces.

   This is exactly the procedure solutions/07-05/zaisrv.bnd's own
   header comment (lines 32-47) already laid out in advance, citing
   work/design/refs/ileconcepts75.txt lines 4287-4289 ("1. Duplicate
   the STRPGMEXP, ENDPGMEXP block that contains PGMLVL(*CURRENT).
   2. Change the duplicated PGMLVL(*CURRENT) value to PGMLVL(*PRV).
   3. In the STRPGMEXP command that contains PGMLVL(*CURRENT), add to
   the end of the list the new symbol"):

     (1) the OLD PGMLVL(*CURRENT) block (GET/RESERVE/RELEASE, in that
         exact order) becomes a NEW PGMLVL(*PRV) block below, unedited
         except for the PGMLVL value - this is what lets any program
         still bound against the 3-symbol signature (e.g. DRIVER,
         solutions/07-05/driver.rpgle, which this lesson deliberately
         does NOT recompile) keep working unchanged.
     (2) the new procedure's EXPORT SYMBOL is appended to the END of
         the PGMLVL(*CURRENT) list - GET/RESERVE/RELEASE keep their
         original relative order, PINGZAISRV is added after them.

   EXPORT SYMBOL('PINGZAISRV'): upper case, no quotes-preserving-case
   trick - matches this file's own established default-casing
   convention (zaisrv.rpgle has no EXTPROC clause on get/reserve/
   release, so RPG exports them upper-case by default; pingZaisrv
   follows the same rule, per solutions/07-05/zaisrv.bnd's own citation
   of ilerpgref75.txt lines 31322-31324/31334-31336/31381-31383).

   STATUS: this file's own claims (successful CRTSRVPGM with this
   4-symbol *CURRENT + 3-symbol *PRV split, and DRIVER continuing to
   run unchanged against the *PRV block) are confirmed separately -
   see docs/probes.md's part08-08-* sections.

   BUILD RECIPE (same two-step path as solutions/07-05/zaisrv.bnd -
   CRTBNDRPG cannot produce a *SRVPGM):
     CRTRPGMOD MODULE(<lib>/ZAISRV) SRCFILE(<lib>/QRPGLESRC)
       SRCMBR(ZAISRV)
     CRTSRVPGM SRVPGM(<lib>/ZAISRV) MODULE(<lib>/ZAISRV)
       EXPORT(*SRCFILE) SRCFILE(<lib>/QSRVSRC) SRCMBR(ZAISRV)
       ACTGRP(*CALLER)
   <lib> is a placeholder for the learner's own library - no real
   PUB400 library or user name appears in this file. */

STRPGMEXP PGMLVL(*CURRENT)
   EXPORT SYMBOL('GET')
   EXPORT SYMBOL('RESERVE')
   EXPORT SYMBOL('RELEASE')
   EXPORT SYMBOL('PINGZAISRV')
ENDPGMEXP

STRPGMEXP PGMLVL(*PRV)
   EXPORT SYMBOL('GET')
   EXPORT SYMBOL('RESERVE')
   EXPORT SYMBOL('RELEASE')
ENDPGMEXP
